  {
   "id": 554364,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2e49c5d240ac148e.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Takuji Ohyama, et al./IntechOpen Book Series, under CC BY 4.0 License)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the amount of nitrogen fixation by a bacterium that lives in and near the roots of the sugar cane plant at different levels of oxygen.</p>\n<p>Based on the \"Fixed N in Bacteria\" line, make a hypothesis about this bacterium.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1090119,
     "content_html": "The bacterium is aerobic."
    },
    {
     "id": 1090120,
     "content_html": "The bacterium is anaerobic."
    },
    {
     "id": 1090121,
     "content_html": "The bacterium is gram-positive."
    },
    {
     "id": 1090122,
     "content_html": "The bacterium is gram-negative."
    }
